Yes, but what I mean is that currently we have something like this:

```go
res := Resources{}
for _, m := range manifests {
  kind := getKind(m)
  switch kind {
  case "ServiceAccount":
    _, _, err := s.Decode(m, nil, &res.ServiceAccount)
  [...]
  }
}
return res
```

My question is what happens if there is two `ServiceAccount` in the `manifests` list? For me, the `_, _, err := s.Decode(m, nil, &res.ServiceAccount)` call will override the first `ServiceAccount` in `res` and we will lose the object content.

Hi,
