**Edit 2**
ok after deleting the operator pod and the clusterpolicy resources were created again in the gpu-operator-resources namespace, I overlooked that when doing Edit 1.

I couldn't reproduce it on purpose now but I might have found something.

We use kubespray for deploying our clusters, when we do a kubespray rollout all nodes are drained and updated in a rolling update.
The rollout happened in 2 clusters in parallel but did only break one of them. After I rebooted one of the nodes in the cluster which was OK after the rollout, it also broke.

