Well, I'm embarrassed to say that the problem ended up being on our end. Turns out that on the one GPU node there was a stale `iptables` chain that was acting as a sink for port 5555, sending packets to a pod IP that no longer existed. It explains why I wasn't seeing any ICMP error messages in the DCGM exporter logs or connection attempts in the DCGM server logs, because the GPU node correctly saw a process listening on the destination port and happily accepted those packets, but then silently dropped them afterwards. After removing the errant chain and redeploying the `gpu-operator`, everything worked fine.

@shivamerla Your `netcat` test was a good suggestion. When that failed with similar behavior it led me to eventually look for firewall and `iptables` issues. Before that I was very much distracted by the ERROR messages in the DCGM server logs. I'm debating about whether to open a separate issue about that, if nothing else at least so that the discussion is documented.

@klueska I will rename this issue to reflect the initial behavior I saw, rather than what I had assumed to be the root cause based on that error.

